+
+## Reproduction gates
+
+1. Build the reachable histories from physical edges. Tabulate every primary frequency/wavelength match and both archived alternative conventions separately. Check both integer signed vectors, the two physical tip ports and the distinct material prefixes.
+2. Check the complete signed detector from the finite seam queries. Apply all seventeen clock settings. Preserve unresolved, malformed and failed settings with their reasons. Reproduce all 32 launches at the sixteen resolved signed settings and the unresolved zero setting. Include the commissioning cap of 96 on all 631 fair operations. Record the launch click, its factor of eight to obtain signed weight, every terminal refusal and the physical port probabilities.
+3. The launch witness must give signed weight above the original 0.98 benchmark. Verify its exact conservation in free evolution and compare launch and return at exposures 1, 7, 37 and 150 to absolute tolerance $2\times10^{-10}$. State a separate simultaneous 99% lower bound from simulated launch counts and the conservative tolerance on the calculated probability.
+4. On the same two preparations, random swaps at the matched hopping rate and sharp-history dephasing must each fall below 0.98 at exposure 37. Test a phase flip at one tip with the two initial occupancies held fixed. Also test whether a commuting dispersion can pass the spectral rule while giving a delocalized positive mode.
+5. In a separate coherent changed-law comparison, retain the actual compiled source and terminal queries. Remove only the degree-five port 9 blank reference during flight. Check that both launch readings agree at zero and that the native and changed-law readings separate at 37. This target-aware adverse comparison was also known before registration.
+6. State whether the independent material and source prescription addresses the selection objection in the M10.4 decision. Report the parked material, the secondary matches and the inconclusive clock. The observable is finite persistence of one dressed load. This task makes no mass, charge, spin, binding or electron-species assignment.
+
+The owner’s public simulation shows how the two-load ancestor’s home probability depends on its eleven records. The present task uses the separate one-load headless read. [Public pair replay](https://floatingpragma.ai/oph/simulation/openwave/row-4/)
